'''Cumará''' is one of the thirteen [[comarca]]s of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. It lies in the southern portion of the province's Shendan-side commuter belt and combines lakefront suburbs, wealthy coastal enclaves, hilly residential districts, and agricultural exurbs. The comarca's capital is [[Varakí]], a large commuter municipality on the high-speed rail corridor to [[Areza]]. In 2026, Cumará had a population of 2,525,000.

The comarca's development is shaped by the corridor between Sant Cristòfor and Areza. [[Costa Serena]] and [[Belljardí]] are affluent residential municipalities, [[La Cruïlla]] and [[Enllaç]] are denser commuter suburbs, and [[Brises, Estret|Brises]], [[Pla dels Pins]], [[Pla dels Horts]], and [[Els Camps]] retain a more rural or semi-rural character. [[Varakí]] is the largest municipality and the main population centre.

== Geography ==

Cumará occupies a broad strip of the southern Shendan coast and the adjoining inland foothills of Estret Province. The western edge is dominated by suburban waterfronts and residential developments, while the inland municipalities become progressively hillier and more agricultural toward the east and south. The comarca's built-up areas cluster around rail stations, road junctions, and the lakefront, while its outer municipalities remain comparatively open.

The comarca covers 1,271.832 km² and has an average density of roughly 1,985 people per km². Population is concentrated most heavily in Varakí and Enllaç, with lower-density residential and agricultural land in the outer municipalities.

