== Demographics ==

Cumará's population is concentrated along the rail and lake corridor, especially in Varakí and Enllaç. The more affluent coastal and park-side municipalities, such as Costa Serena and Belljardí, have comparatively high residential values, while Brises, Els Camps, and the outer inland districts remain much more sparsely settled. The comarca is dominated by suburban and commuter housing, with only a handful of municipalities retaining strongly rural patterns.

== Economy ==

The economy of Cumará is based on commuting, residential services, education, and local retail. Varakí functions as the comarca's principal service centre and the main gateway to the high-speed rail line, while La Cruïlla and Enllaç support dense commuter housing and transit-oriented development. Costa Serena's private university and affluent residential stock make it one of the comarca's prestige areas, while the outer municipalities still support agriculture, small-scale farming, and exurban housing.

== Transport ==

Cumará is served by the high-speed rail corridor between Sant Cristòfor and Areza, with Varakí as the principal rail hub. Costa Serena also has a commuter rail station, and Enllaç is an important transit-oriented suburban node. Road connections link the comarca's municipalities with Sant Cristòfor, Areza, and the rest of Estret Province, while local bus routes provide secondary connections between the lakefront, the hillside districts, and the suburban edge.

== History ==

Cumará developed as the southern suburban counterpart to Sant Cristòfor's metropolitan growth. The oldest settlements were coastal and lake-adjacent communities, but much of the comarca's present form dates from later commuter expansion, when rail and road links made it possible for residents to live in hill suburbs, gated coastal enclaves, and semi-rural districts while working in Sant Cristòfor or Areza. The high-speed rail corridor further strengthened Varakí and the surrounding lakefront belt as the comarca's main population axis.

